(3750895, 519937, 66597, '<td valign="top">An interesting entry that certainly fits science very well! I like how you used color temp to your advantage to give an overall warm feel. You may have gotten hurt by some of the extra beakers, etc. in the background - there''s a lot of details to take in here. Still, a most creative and worthy entry!</td>', 'An interesting entry that certainly fits science very well! I like how you used color temp to your advantage to give an overall warm feel. You may have gotten hurt by some of the extra beakers, etc. in the background - there''s a lot of details to take in here. Still, a most creative and worthy entry!', '2007-06-07 09:45:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3751751, 523262, 12998, '<td valign="top">The pole is somewhat distracting, could have cropped some of it out.  Both birds look somewhat out of focus.  The white breast of the flying bird looks to be over exposed, you might have over corrected this if you post processed the picture.<br/> <br/>I like the content of the picture.  Moving closer might have helped but you probably were restricted as to how close you could get.</td>', 'The pole is somewhat distracting, could have cropped some of it out.  Both birds look somewhat out of focus.  The white breast of the flying bird looks to be over exposed, you might have over corrected this if you post processed the picture. I like the content of the picture.  Moving closer might have helped but you probably were restricted as to how close you could get.', '2007-06-07 13:47:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3751775, 523262, 5885, '<td valign="top">Compositionally boring. Cropping right below the nest would have added much more impact. Placing the mother and the baby on thirds intersections would have made it even stronger.<br/> <br/>Lighting is somewhat flat, but playing with curves could have added some punch.</td>', 'Compositionally boring. Cropping right below the nest would have added much more impact. Placing the mother and the baby on thirds intersections would have made it even stronger. Lighting is somewhat flat, but playing with curves could have added some punch.', '2007-06-07 13:55:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3751807, 523262, 51802, '<td valign="top">I did not vote on this challenge, but I would probably have given this a 5.  It meets the challenge, it is an interesting capture, but not overall impressive.  Some things that hurt it are the lack of contrast, and the composition.  The sky really put you at a disadvantage.  Being hazy gives the picture an overall dullness which there is not much you could have done about.  I think a much closer crop would help this though.  If you had filled the bottom of the frame with the nest it would have made the viewer feel like he was much closer to the action.  However, if you have already cropped off a lot, you may run into resolution problems.  A 5 tells me that there is nothing really bad about the picture, but there are flaws that prevent it from being a great picture.</td>', 'I did not vote on this challenge, but I would probably have given this a 5.  It meets the challenge, it is an interesting capture, but not overall impressive.  Some things that hurt it are the lack of contrast, and the composition.  The sky really put you at a disadvantage.  Being hazy gives the picture an overall dullness which there is not much you could have done about.  I think a much closer crop would help this though.  If you had filled the bottom of the frame with the nest it would have made the viewer feel like he was much closer to the action.  However, if you have already cropped off a lot, you may run into resolution problems.  A 5 tells me that there is nothing really bad about the picture, but there are flaws that prevent it from being a great picture.', '2007-06-07 14:06:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3751810, 523262, 39560, '<td valign="top">It looks as though your 70-200 didn''t have enough reach and you are cropping in closer. The colors seem to be washed out. Focus is off. Subject matter would be OK if you could''ve gotten closer and I would''ve also cropped the pole out.</td>', 'It looks as though your 70-200 didn''t have enough reach and you are cropping in closer. The colors seem to be washed out. Focus is off. Subject matter would be OK if you could''ve gotten closer and I would''ve also cropped the pole out.', '2007-06-07 14:07:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3751887, 521110, 52549, '<td valign="top">Stunning shot! Big congrats on 5th place.</td>', 'Stunning shot! Big congrats on 5th place.', '2007-06-07 14:28:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3752297, 523262, 61559, '<td valign="top">GREAT capture. Very high degree of difficulty!</td>', 'GREAT capture. Very high degree of difficulty!', '2007-06-07 15:51:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3752644, 520911, 5792, '<td valign="top"><b>Positives:</b> <br/>Stunning clarity, good color and a nice macro. Good concept. <br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/>You didn''t say in the notes, but imply that this was captured through a microscope. You probably need a lensed adapter to prevent REAL vignetting. LOL!!! You can always deal with that problem through cropping, though.<br/> <br/>Lighting(away from the vignette), sharpness are exceptional.<br/> <br/>The image lacks a central focal object for the human eye to latch onto. It is like a really nice background without a main subject.<br/> <br/><b>The Challenge:</b> <br/>Yup... science all right. :) It placed well and scored above average. This undoutably is because of it''s superb technical quality. But the composition itself lacked thematic content or eye attractive viewpoints and that held the score down.  <br/> <br/><b>Suggestions:</b> <br/>The image, as it is is fine, but it needs more sharply focused chives positioned in more interesting ways... whatever THAT means. ;) How to do it is another story all together. I doubt you have any control over DOF so that makes that a very difficult job. Just keep moving things around until to get a lot of chive in focus in an interesting arrangement. :)<br/> <br/>For less vignette simply crop the image closer. Detail will be larger in the frame and your camera provides plenty of data for you to work with.</td>', 'Positives: Stunning clarity, good color and a nice macro. Good concept.  Technicals: You didn''t say in the notes, but imply that this was captured through a microscope. You probably need a lensed adapter to prevent REAL vignetting. LOL!!! You can always deal with that problem through cropping, though. Lighting(away from the vignette), sharpness are exceptional. The image lacks a central focal object for the human eye to latch onto. It is like a really nice background without a main subject. The Challenge: Yup... science all right. :) It placed well and scored above average. This undoutably is because of it''s superb technical quality. But the composition itself lacked thematic content or eye attractive viewpoints and that held the score down.   Suggestions: The image, as it is is fine, but it needs more sharply focused chives positioned in more interesting ways... whatever THAT means. ;) How to do it is another story all together. I doubt you have any control over DOF so that makes that a very difficult job. Just keep moving things around until to get a lot of chive in focus in an interesting arrangement. :) For less vignette simply crop the image closer. Detail will be larger in the frame and your camera provides plenty of data for you to work with.', '2007-06-07 17:27:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3752662, 520306, 79006, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jahoward:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the concept.  Why did you choose to desaturate certain parts of the photograph? </i></td></tr></table> The photo was real yellow from the flourcent lights and the slow shutter speed.</td>', 'Originally posted by jahoward: I like the concept.  Why did you choose to desaturate certain parts of the photograph?  The photo was real yellow from the flourcent lights and the slow shutter speed.', '2007-06-07 17:32:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3752862, 523262, 44878, '<td valign="top">I think its a very good Photo and definately worthy of a Higher Mark as youhave suggested.<br/>To Be honest, although I find nothing wrong with your Photo at all, the voters have probably thought - Oh not another Osprey Photo !<br/>How ever, Dont let it bother you.<br/>As long as you think under the Circumstances, you gt the Best Possible Picture you could, then be proud.<br/> <br/>Cheers.<br/>Joe</td>', 'I think its a very good Photo and definately worthy of a Higher Mark as youhave suggested.To Be honest, although I find nothing wrong with your Photo at all, the voters have probably thought - Oh not another Osprey Photo !How ever, Dont let it bother you.As long as you think under the Circumstances, you gt the Best Possible Picture you could, then be proud. Cheers.Joe', '2007-06-07 18:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
